{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495533-how-many-times-have-you-been-to-the-convention-of-thorns","id":1495533,"title":"How many times have you been to the Convention of Thorns?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-24T12:25:44-07:00","id":1495533,"title":"How many times have you been to the Convention of Thorns?","content":"So, I just interviewed my Storyteller for Transylvania Chronicles for my podcast and I realized that soon, I will have been to the Convention of Thorns 4 times<br /> <br /> The first time was the first time I ever played Vampire: the Masquerade. Our Storyteller started the game in the Middle Ages (this was way before Dark Ages was published - we'd played a lot of Ars Magica) and we obviously attended the Convention fo Thorns. I remember very little about it, except our Malkavian character becoming the first Malkavian Justicar and the Ventrue dacning with someone to the music of a supernatually skilled violinist.<br /> <br /> Second time was when we played Transylvania Chronicles for the first time. Our ST wrote out the text of the convention on vellum-looking paper using a calligraphy pen and all the players signed in-character. The Tzimisce character managed to get it written into the convention that Tremeres could not be princes, as a punishment for their diablerie of Saulot.<br /> <br /> The third time was the first Convention of Thorns LARP and it was AMAZING! Loved it so much. I played a Gangrel who ended up promised the position as Justicar.<br /> <br /> And now, I am played Transylvania Chronicles again and will soon attend, this time as Lasombra sort-of Anarch. Our coterie will definately join the Sabbat. It'll be fun to see it from that point of view.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T20:08:44-07:00","id":1495545,"title":"","content":"Zero times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-24-2022, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T16:21:40-07:00","id":1495791,"title":"","content":"Twice.<br /> <br /> It was fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T09:10:21-07:00","id":1495832,"title":"","content":"Zero times as none of my characters I ever made were that old and my character's grandsire is a just barely an elder at 315 years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T03:40:28-07:00","id":1496182,"title":"","content":"Not once for me. But then again I'm more into Dark Ages so I'm mostly interested in playing before the Anarch Revolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T11:23:49-07:00","id":1496208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495533-how-many-times-have-you-been-to-the-convention-of-thorns?p=1495791#post1495791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twice.<br /> <br /> It was fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it the same (or at least comperable) kind of fun, enjoyment, and satisfaction during each of the two instances your players' characters paricipated in the Convention of Thorns?<br /> Also - were the players active participants in some way, or did the simply observe the Convention of Throns with some separation or distance? While perhaps trying to change, influence, or benefit from the event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T19:25:52-07:00","id":1496237,"title":"","content":"I've ran it once, not too long ago.<br /> It was fun, I made a voting system for each matter in debate. With two extra matters to decide besides the ones already present. <br /> Cuz otherwise my players wouldn't interact with the Convention. So with votes, they could try to bribe, blackmail, make speeches or background talks, through Tests. And sometimes they did engaged with it very closely, and some decisions were a bit different than from canon, but not too much.<br /> <br /> Its worth mentioning that I ran the Convention with two groups, The coterie from Transylvania Chronicles (in our game, called the Georgian Rooks) and the Children of Isaac (from Giovanni Chronicles). Both being played by their player. To do that each session we would change the POV to the other group. It was cool, and sometimes both groups would fight for votes on their preferred sides. While the Rooks were practically Elders, and the Ventrue a descendant of Hardestadt, one of the Children of Isaac was an Archon, under Hardestadt, but they hate each other in-game, but are played by different players.<br /> <br /> It is a very nice event, but unfortunately my players weren't interested in politicking or interacting that much in here, which was a shame. I was expecting some very nice treaties and negotiations, but there weren't, they were pretty passive all in all. And changing the course of history is something I always look at the Convention being a branching point. But a lot of cool characters were there, and some interesting sightings happened too. <br /> Gotson, the Lasombra was there. Hardestadt acting a bit melancholic when in the same space as the widow Rosamund. A delegation from the Ashirra. One of the sires from the Children of Isaac being burned alive while giving a martyr's speech that would be part of the Sabbat... <br /> <br /> Wasn't as grand, incredible and significant as I hoped, but I kind of had way too big expectations. But it was cool, undeniably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T17:05:27-08:00","id":1496343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495533-how-many-times-have-you-been-to-the-convention-of-thorns?p=1496208#post1496208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was it the same (or at least comperable) kind of fun, enjoyment, and satisfaction during each of the two instances your players' characters paricipated in the Convention of Thorns?<br /> Also - were the players active participants in some way, or did the simply observe the Convention of Throns with some separation or distance? While perhaps trying to change, influence, or benefit from the event?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I usually do it as a Transylvania Chronicles follow-up or a sequel to the Dark Ages, I make it so that the player characters attending the Convention of Thorns are people who are VERY IMPORTANT to what is happening to it. I let the players even state what sort of role they would be taking but I have often come up with some general ideas to pass their way as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch Founder/Sabbat Founder</b>: The player characters can be revolutionaries of the First Anarch Revolt. They're either there to surrender because the Camarilla has won the contest or because they actually think the concessions they've gotten out of the Elders are decent enough to justify it. The player characters will be offered opportunities to betray their fellow Anarchs, join High Society, or possibly decide that the surrender agreement is bullshit because Hardelstadt plans to start walking back his promises as soon as the Convention is over.<br /> <br /> <b>Reformers</b>: The Camarilla is something I present as things the player characters might found actually as a way to IMPROVE vampire society. They don't have to just be Elders or the pawns of Elders (but they can be). The Camarilla can guarantee things like freedom of movement, the Masquerade, and making it illegal to automatically blood bond your progeny or forbid Princes from killing without cause. All things that the Elders are reluctant to agree to but were there in writing.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silchester Massacre</b>: I actually have had plenty of player characters decide to continue the Anarch Revolt but only to find their fellow remaining Anarchs plan to show their contempt for mortals as well as the Masquerade by killing every single man, woman, and child in Silchester. Which I tend to use to not have the player characters become monsters but to have this reaction instead.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/vzrYP4mKYA4AAAAC/i-have-made-huge-mistake.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T07:00:29-08:00","id":1496491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495533-how-many-times-have-you-been-to-the-convention-of-thorns?p=1496343#post1496343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since I usually do it as a Transylvania Chronicles follow-up or a sequel to the Dark Ages, I make it so that the player characters attending the Convention of Thorns are people who are VERY IMPORTANT to what is happening to it. I let the players even state what sort of role they would be taking but I have often come up with some general ideas to pass their way as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Anarch Founder/Sabbat Founder</b>: The player characters can be revolutionaries of the First Anarch Revolt. They're either there to surrender because the Camarilla has won the contest or because they actually think the concessions they've gotten out of the Elders are decent enough to justify it. The player characters will be offered opportunities to betray their fellow Anarchs, join High Society, or possibly decide that the surrender agreement is bullshit because Hardelstadt plans to start walking back his promises as soon as the Convention is over.<br /> <br /> <b>Reformers</b>: The Camarilla is something I present as things the player characters might found actually as a way to IMPROVE vampire society. They don't have to just be Elders or the pawns of Elders (but they can be). The Camarilla can guarantee things like freedom of movement, the Masquerade, and making it illegal to automatically blood bond your progeny or forbid Princes from killing without cause. All things that the Elders are reluctant to agree to but were there in writing.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silchester Massacre</b>: I actually have had plenty of player characters decide to continue the Anarch Revolt but only to find their fellow remaining Anarchs plan to show their contempt for mortals as well as the Masquerade by killing every single man, woman, and child in Silchester. Which I tend to use to not have the player characters become monsters but to have this reaction instead.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/vzrYP4mKYA4AAAAC/i-have-made-huge-mistake.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the elaboration, this looks like a good, interesting, complex, and nice approach.<br /> <br /> Have you ever give any though or consideration to possibly including Vampires from the Tal'Mahe'Ra Sect in the Convention of Thorns, or in situations stemming from this event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T09:34:16-08:00","id":1496504,"title":"","content":"In my Transyl.Chronicles, two secretly TalMaheRa fellows, one of them being Jalan A'ajav, participated on the Raid of the Eldest Haven, although not taking part in the diablerie nor entering the inner sanctum. Cuz in my game, I made the body of the Eldest be that awesome artwork of a big armored fellow made of bones and flesh (I think its from the Gehenna book), so when Lugoj started to drain the Eldest, his blood started pouring out like a torrent, down the stairs, into the floor, and every one but Lambach who fled in terror, felt into a crazy frenzy and drank the Eldest's blood, lowering one Generation freely.<br /> And both these TalMaheRa fellows were in the Convention, as testimony mostly, not talking much, but making some speeches among the Anarchs. They did help make diversions secretly, so that the unbowing Anarchs that would attack Silchester could escape. So yeah, I think its fun to put the agents behind the scenes, scheming, being mysterious and swaying some things without no one knowing about it. <br /> <br /> I made the Camarilla be composed of some different groups, initially for the votes on the Convention, but then to simulate a bit of the dynamics on V.Requiem that I thinks is missing from Masquerade. There are those that want a real Masquerade lockdown, happy to give powers to the Justicars and Cam. officials as to punish detractors of the Sect. There are those that want Camarilla to be a hedonic society of elite, grandeur and debauchery, like bloody baroque aristocrats that are very quick to accept the purge of undesirables and love a good show. Then there are those that are like the Council of Scales, the Prometheans and all that, which are the reformers, pro-humanity. There are also the elders and their childer who think the sect should be a big cult for elders, that shouldn't have to bow their heads to any bigger authority in the Camarilla; they also fully and subtlety believe in Gehenna and fear it as all hell. The in-between and less extreme are sub-groups. <br /> <br /> Also, in Thorns the Tremere after making a magic oath swearing to not use for anything else, took the blood of the Banu Haqim after the agreements on the treaty. Then they made a ritual that transported the blood vials to where Tremere himself was. But it will only be used to make the curse after the Treaty of Tyre. The Banu Haqim in North Africa and Middle East, mostly the Ashirra are running against the clock to try and destroy the Baali or dispell their original curse, cuz they fear having to suffer both at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T10:26:01-08:00","id":1496509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495533-how-many-times-have-you-been-to-the-convention-of-thorns?p=1496491#post1496491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the elaboration, this looks like a good, interesting, complex, and nice approach.<br /> <br /> Have you ever give any though or consideration to possibly including Vampires from the Tal'Mahe'Ra Sect in the Convention of Thorns, or in situations stemming from this event?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the Tal'Mah'Ra in my games is that it is a downplayed version of the one from DSOTBH. It is a powerful Gehenna Cult, perhaps THE most powerful Gehenna Cult, but it is also just one faction among many and has the primary goal of shit stirring among vampires that is not terribly difficult to begin with. It's probable and even likely that there were Black Hand agents among the Anarch and Camarilla delegates both but they wouldn't be advertising their membership. There's probably also an Inconnu or two watching events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}